Eigen source files are covered by MPL 2.0 at file level: the files under src/prosdk/thirdparty/eigen
are vendored unmodified apart from the include-path rewrite, the Arduino macro guard, the
configuration include (tools/upstream/wpilib.py) and the patches in tools/upstream/patches/eigen,
and their source is this repository.

Two driver libraries are vendored by hand, not by tools/upstream/wpilib.py:
- The Melexis MLX90640 and MLX90641 API, from https://github.com/melexis/mlx90640-library
  (commit f6be7ca1) and https://github.com/melexis/mlx90641-library (commit 3c94aa87). Each
  modified file keeps the upstream license header and carries a "Modified by Probot Studio"
  notice that lists the changes (MLX90640_API.c renamed to .cpp, namespace prosdk::melexis,
  include paths, line endings; the upstream I2C layer replaced by
  src/prosdk/drivers/thermal/melexis/MelexisI2C.*).
- The ST VL53L7CX Ultra Lite Driver 2.0.0, from https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/x-cube-tof1
  (Drivers/BSP/Components/vl53l7cx/modules, commit 9d721708c394de16aaee9d1579e1f79f2a1e085a),
  unmodified. Its platform layer (platform.h, platform.cpp, VL53L7CXPlatform.hpp in the same
  folder) is hand-written.

The examples in examples/ and their tests in test/examples are ported by hand from WPILib's
wpilibcExamples with the same renames (design/examples.md). Each keeps upstream's copyright
lines; tools/upstream/examples.json records the upstream files and their git blob ids at the
pinned commit.

